From: well0nez <8986239+well0nez@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: misc: hy310-board-mgr: thermal-shutdown per board, an orderly power off

The NTC's power off was armed only by the module parameter
thermal_shutdown, which arms it on every board, and it called
kernel_power_off(): no userspace shutdown, the file systems not unmounted.

- A board's tree arms it for that board alone with the boolean property
  thermal-shutdown in the board manager's node - for the L018 once its NTC
  has been held against a thermometer; the parameter stays and still arms
  it everywhere.
- The power off goes the way of the fan stall: orderly_poweroff(true),
  once, with a dev_emerg line that names the temperature and the
  threshold. The stock firmware leaves it to Android after a
  TEMP_STATE=SHUTDOWN uevent (pwm_fan.c, read off the L018's stock kernel
  25.10.2026); no userspace listens for that here.

No tree sets thermal-shutdown yet, so nothing changes on any board until
one does; with the parameter set the power off is now orderly instead of
immediate. Built in the h713-build container. Not measured: the NTC has
not been near a power off threshold on any board.

diff -ruN a/drivers/misc/hy310-board-mgr.c b/drivers/misc/hy310-board-mgr.c
--- a/drivers/misc/hy310-board-mgr.c
+++ b/drivers/misc/hy310-board-mgr.c
@@ -131,6 +131,10 @@
  * table. What is still missing is the comparison of the curve against a
  * reference thermometer on the device; until then the driver only reports and warns.
  * Set thermal_shutdown=1 only once temp1_input has been measured on the device.
+ *
+ * A board's tree can arm it for that board alone with the boolean property
+ * thermal-shutdown in the board manager's node, once its NTC has been held
+ * against a thermometer; the parameter arms it everywhere.
  */
 static bool thermal_shutdown;
 module_param(thermal_shutdown, bool, 0644);
@@ -303,6 +307,8 @@
 
 	/* Set once a poweroff has been requested, so it is requested only once */
 	bool			 poweroff_started;
+	/* thermal-shutdown in the tree, or the parameter */
+	bool			 thermal_shutdown;
 	/* jiffies: the fan rail came back at resume, no stall verdict before */
 	unsigned long		 fan_judge_after;
 
@@ -839,16 +845,26 @@
 			priv->ntc.poweroff_cycles, NTC_POWEROFF_CYCLES);
 
 		if (priv->ntc.poweroff_cycles >= NTC_POWEROFF_CYCLES) {
-			if (!thermal_shutdown) {
+			if (!priv->thermal_shutdown && !thermal_shutdown) {
 				/* Report once per crossing, then keep counting. */
 				if (priv->ntc.poweroff_cycles == NTC_POWEROFF_CYCLES)
 					dev_err(priv->dev,
 						"NTC: thermal emergency (shutdown disabled, set thermal_shutdown=1 to arm)\n");
 			} else {
-				dev_err(priv->dev,
-					"NTC: thermal emergency, initiating poweroff\n");
-				kernel_power_off();
-				return;
+				/*
+				 * As at a stalled fan: userspace gets its shutdown (the
+				 * file systems are synced and unmounted), the force flag
+				 * makes sure a wedged userspace does not keep a hot box
+				 * running. The stock firmware leaves it to Android, after
+				 * a TEMP_STATE=SHUTDOWN uevent; here nobody would listen.
+				 */
+				if (!priv->poweroff_started) {
+					priv->poweroff_started = true;
+					dev_emerg(priv->dev,
+						  "NTC: thermal emergency, %d C above %d C -- powering off\n",
+						  temp_c, priv->temp_poweroff_c);
+					orderly_poweroff(true);
+				}
 			}
 		}
 	} else {
@@ -1416,6 +1432,7 @@
 		priv->temp_warn_c = DEFAULT_TEMP_WARN_C;
 	if (of_property_read_u32(np, "temp_resume", &priv->temp_resume_c))
 		priv->temp_resume_c = INT_MIN;
+	priv->thermal_shutdown = of_property_read_bool(np, "thermal-shutdown");
 
 	/* ---- ntc subnode: enable, source and channel ---- */
 	priv->ntc_source = HY310_NTC_SOURCE_GPADC;
